# Issue Workflow

Topology (slots, ephemeral `feature/*`, shared-core): [`docs/handoffs/worktree-branch-topology.md`](../../docs/handoffs/worktree-branch-topology.md).

| Condition | Workflow |
|-----------|----------|
| Modules overlap another **ready** issue, or change touches **shared core** | **Isolate** — one issue at a time |
| Unblocked and path-disjoint from other ready issues | **Parallel** — one worktree per **task** (not a permanent FE/BE lane) |

**Shared core** (never bundle into a feature PR): canonical list in the topology handoff (`packages/contracts`, root workspace/CI config, canonical `docs/architecture/*`, `CONTEXT.md`, …). Land a dedicated PR first. `packages/contracts` is FE-owned until an OpenAPI/codegen ADR.

## Parallel pipeline (no blocked)

Per issue, independently:

`implement` → Review Agent (`intent-review` → `guardrails` → `validate`) → commit → open **individual** PR → PR **fast CI** (path-filtered lint/type/cheap tests) → **GitHub Merge Queue** (`merge_group` full suite) → merge

Do **not** batch parallel work into one PR. Path-disjoint issues stay on separate branches/PRs.

Path-disjoint **product** PRs may **auto-enqueue** to Merge Queue after Review Agent passes and PR fast CI is green. **Human approval** required before enqueue/merge for **shared-core**, **auth**, **prod-config**, and **public-release** changes.

### Sync-before-merge (fallback — cutover only)

Use when Merge Queue is **unavailable** (cutover, outage, or **user-owned repo** — GitHub MQ requires an org-owned repository; see topology handoff). Rebase (or merge) onto **current** `origin/main` immediately before merge, push (`--force-with-lease` if rebased), confirm CI green again, then merge directly. Prefer Merge Queue once the repo is org-owned and the queue is enabled.

## GitHub ops (parallel runs)

- One agent holds the ops lock in the active `docs/handoffs/parallel-status.md` (create/update per parallel run).
- Ops owner alone: `git push`, `gh pr create|merge|checks`, Merge Queue enqueue, issue close on `main`.
- Others: commit locally; stagger remote ops ≥ **30s**.
